  "details": "Would be fun to use a tracker (Vive, Tundra etc.) to control the position of a toggleable item (pet, beverage, tools, furniture, etc) on an avatar.\n\nIn SteamVR settings we usually set dedicated roles to individual trackers (left foot, hip, right elbow, etc) so we just set no particular role.\n\nVRC could then detect and use specifically those unassigned trackers, list them up in the option menu tracking/ik section and let players assign them to a tracked item withing the VRC options menu. (LHR-1234ABCD -> TrackedItem_01, LHR-ABCD1234 -> TrackedItem_02, etc.)\n\nIn the avatar SDK we could define tracked objects by putting them into an empty object in the avatar's root, attaching a specific SDK script/object to that container including the aforementioned nametags which appear in VRCs tracking/ik menu.\n\nThe object would be tracked in default playspace, toggling the object on/off via the usual animation system from within the usual expressions menu would simply hide and deactivate the tracking.\n\nThis idea is inspired by stepped-on dog tails, gallons of spilled beer, by a dead thread from 2018 and of course by Jangxx's VRC-tracked-objects, which is a cool and much appreciated attempt but sadly way too janky and has too many limitations as we can see in a youtube video by ChrisQuitsReality/Kermies.\n\nCheers!",
